content.text:
In RTL direction (`html[dir="rtl"]`), VitePress's default `.VPFlyout .menu` stylesheet hardcoded `right: 0`, aligning the dropdown's right rail with the trigger button. Because header elements flip to the left side under RTL layout, this caused the menu to expand leftward and overflow off the viewport edge.

Added an RTL override in [docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css](docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css#L393-L399):

```css
/* In RTL layouts, navbar flyouts (language dropdown, extra/theme picker, etc.) sit on the left side
   of the header. VitePress defaults flyout menus to `right: 0`, which aligns their right edge to the
   icon and causes the menu to overflow off the left edge of the page. Align to the left rail instead. */
html[dir="rtl"] .VPFlyout .menu {
  right: auto;
  left: 0;
}
```

The dropdown now aligns its left rail to the trigger button in RTL mode, expanding inward toward the page center without overflowing.
